.TH "JRING" "1" "" "jring" "User Commands"
.SH "NAME"
jring \- privacy\-first Linux client for explicitly selected JRing devices
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B jring
[global options] command [command options]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
JRing is offline by default and does not scan, connect, write, or emit desktop input unless the matching command and explicit authorization gate are supplied. Generated help never probes Bluetooth or the host.
Privacy\-first JRing Linux client
.SH "COMMANDS"
.TP
.B doctor
passively check local simulator and hardware prerequisites
.TP
.B input\-actions
list local simulator events and allowlisted input actions
.TP
.B tui
open a safe, simulator\-first terminal menu (no device selected)
.TP
.B completion
print an installed shell completion script
.TP
.B protocol\-coverage
inspect offline APK\-to\-Python parity without Bluetooth
.TP
.B non\-health\-capabilities
list offline non\-health, HID, sensor, and input candidates
.TP
.B input
simulator\-only preview or emission; live ring events are unavailable
.TP
.B discover
actively scan with explicit consent; redacts addresses and never connects
.TP
.B pair
pair one selected device through local BlueZ (never trusts it)
.TP
.B status
read battery, device information, and capabilities
.TP
.B capabilities
inventory standard HID and known vendor metadata without reading values
.TP
.B heart\-rate
collect one bounded standard Heart Rate notification
.TP
.B time\-sync
write standard Bluetooth Current Time
.TP
.B history
export history (simulator only until verified)
.TP
.B verify\-device\-info
run one owner\-hardware device\-info transport canary
.TP
.B observe
privately collect bounded unknown notifications from one explicit metadata target
.TP
.B review\-observation
review one private observation without Bluetooth I/O
.TP
.B review\-owner\-evidence
review one private owner\-evidence record without Bluetooth I/O
.TP
.B derive\-owner\-evidence
create one sanitized public compatibility row without Bluetooth I/O
